# Local dev bindings for `npx wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored — secrets never get committed.
#
# WITHOUT the Hyperdrive binding (local dev), this worker resolves the live
# DATABASE_URL from the Heroku Platform API — never preset, rotation heals.
#
# HEROKU_APP_NAME  — "mawzun" (plain text)
# HEROKU_API_TOKEN — local dev: output of `heroku auth:token`
#                    prod: create once with `heroku authorizations:create`,
#                    set as a Secret (not a Variable) in Cloudflare.
# DATABASE_SSL     — "1" forces TLS on the resolved URL (auto-detected from
#                    the URL's sslmode in most cases; set for local tunnels).
# DB_URL_TTL_MS    — resolver cache TTL (default 300000 = 5 min).
# APP_SECRET       — HKDF key that unseals Shopify-style secrets read from the
#                    DB (must EXACTLY match the backend's APP_SECRET).
#
# --- Hyperdrive in local dev ------------------------------------------------
# `wrangler dev` refuses to start when the HYPERDRIVE binding has no local
# Postgres to talk to. It reads the local connection string from the PROCESS
# ENVIRONMENT, not from this file — setting it here has no effect, which is a
# trap worth knowing before you spend an hour on it. Export it on the command
# line instead (PowerShell shown; use `export` in bash):
#
#   $env:CLOUDFLARE_HYPERDRIVE_LOCAL_CONNECTION_STRING_HYPERDRIVE = "<DATABASE_URL>"
#   npx wrangler dev --port 8791
#
# Use the backend's restricted-role DATABASE_URL so row-level security behaves
# the same locally as in production. Never paste the owner URL here: the owner
# bypasses RLS, so a local run against it would silently pass tests that the
# deployed worker would fail.
HEROKU_APP_NAME=mawzun
HEROKU_API_TOKEN=
# DATABASE_SSL=1
# DB_URL_TTL_MS=300000
APP_SECRET=

# --- AI per-key throttle (Layerbase Redis REST) — src/ratelimit.ts -----------
# Layerbase's REST endpoint is Upstash-compatible; both spellings work:
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / REDIS_REST_URL and UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN /
# REDIS_REST_TOKEN. Unset = fail-open (no enforcement) + one warning per
# isolate. Kill switch: AI_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=0/false/no = off.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://<your-rest-url>
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=<your-rest-token>
# Per-key overrides (set on the API-keys screen, null = these defaults):
AI_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=600
AI_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# AI_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=0
